/** \page cmake-presets Building with CMake Presets

Navigate back: \ref index "Main" / \ref Cookbook
<hr>

\section sec_cmake_presets_build Building HDF5 with CMake Presets

\par Problem
You want a repeatable configure, build, test, and package command for a
supported HDF5 source-build environment.

\par Supported environments
The HDF5 source tree accepts these combinations:
\li Windows x64 with MSVC 18 and the Visual Studio 18 2026 generator.
\li Linux x86_64 with GCC/G++ and the Ninja or Unix Makefiles generator.

The presets supplied by the project use Visual Studio 18 2026 on Windows and
Ninja on Linux. Other platform, compiler, architecture, and generator
combinations are not supported for building HDF5.

\par Available root workflows
The root <a href="https://\SRCURL/CMakePresets.json"><tt>CMakePresets.json</tt></a>
provides these public workflows:
\li <tt>ci-StdShar-MSVC</tt> - Windows x64/MSVC standard workflow.
\li <tt>ci-StdShar-GNUC</tt> - Linux x86_64/GCC standard workflow.
\li <tt>ci-StdShar-GNUC-S3</tt> - Linux x86_64/GCC workflow with ROS3.

Each workflow configures, builds, tests, and creates a package. The standard
settings build the C and C++ libraries, tools, examples, compression support,
and configured plugins. See the preset JSON for the exact inherited cache
variables.

\par List presets
Run this command from the HDF5 source directory:
\code
cmake --list-presets=all
\endcode

Configure presets are conditioned on the host platform. Therefore the Windows
preset is visible as a configure preset on Windows and the GNU presets are
visible as configure presets on Linux.

\par Run a workflow
On Windows:
\code
cmake --workflow --preset ci-StdShar-MSVC --fresh
\endcode

On Linux:
\code
cmake --workflow --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC --fresh
\endcode

For the Linux ROS3 configuration:
\code
cmake --workflow --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC-S3 --fresh
\endcode

The preset build and install locations are:
\li <tt>&lt;source-parent&gt;/build/&lt;preset-name&gt;</tt>
\li <tt>&lt;source-parent&gt;/install/&lt;preset-name&gt;</tt>

\subsection subsec_cmake_presets_steps Running Individual Steps

The configure, build, test, and package presets use the same public names:
\code
cmake --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC --fresh
cmake --build --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC
ctest --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC
cpack --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC
\endcode

Use <tt>ci-StdShar-MSVC</tt> in the same commands on Windows. The retained
project presets limit builds to six jobs and tests to four jobs.

\subsection subsec_cmake_presets_custom Customizing a Build

For a one-time change, append cache options to the configure command:
\code
cmake --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC -DHDF5_BUILD_CPP_LIB=OFF
\endcode

For repeatable local settings, create <tt>CMakeUserPresets.json</tt> beside
<tt>CMakePresets.json</tt>. Inherit only from the preset family for the current
supported environment:
\li <tt>ci-x64-Release-MSVC</tt> or <tt>ci-StdShar-MSVC</tt> on Windows.
\li <tt>ci-x64-Release-GNUC</tt> or <tt>ci-StdShar-GNUC</tt> on Linux.

Do not commit a user preset that contains machine-specific paths. A user preset
does not bypass HDF5's platform/compiler validation.

\subsection subsec_cmake_presets_examples Standalone Example Presets

The retained standalone projects under <tt>HDF5Examples</tt> have their own
<tt>CMakePresets.json</tt>. They provide:
\li <tt>ci-StdShar-MSVC</tt> on Windows x64/MSVC.
\li <tt>ci-StdShar-GNUC</tt> on Linux x86_64/GCC.

The example workflows configure, build, and test against an HDF5 package. They
do not define package presets:
\code
cd HDF5Examples
cmake --workflow --preset ci-StdShar-GNUC --fresh
\endcode

Use <tt>ci-StdShar-MSVC</tt> on Windows. Set <tt>HDF5_ROOT</tt> or
<tt>CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH</tt> when the installed package is not in a default
search location.

\subsection subsec_cmake_presets_files Preset File Layout

The public root file includes
<tt>config/cmake-presets/hidden-presets.json</tt>. The hidden file owns common
directories, configurations, compiler selection, generator selection, job
limits, and the retained MSVC AddressSanitizer building blocks. The public root
file composes those blocks with compression, examples, plugins, C++, and ROS3
settings.

The GNU toolchain preset selects
<tt>config/toolchain/gcc.cmake</tt>. The MSVC preset selects the Visual Studio
18 2026 generator and x64 architecture directly.

\par See Also
\li <a href="https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/manual/cmake-presets.7.html">CMake preset documentation</a>
\li <a href="https://\SRCURL/docs/INSTALL_CMake.md"><tt>INSTALL_CMake.md</tt></a>
\li <a href="https://\SRCURL/docs/INSTALL_CMake_options.md"><tt>INSTALL_CMake_options.md</tt></a>

